DESCRIPTION The migration run as a saga: communication, coordination and consistency, chosen explicitly (K12)
CATEGORY Integration
NAMESPACE EtlRWorkflowsNS
DEFINE SYSTEM ETL-R AS etl-r-implementations-on-gcp
     # one run = the eight stages of spec/PIPELINE.md:
     # extract gate intake curate enrich produce load recon
     DEFINE SAGA Migration Run Saga AS
          # the runner launches and watches every stage job, in order
          DEFINE COMMUNICATION Orchestrator TO Stage Jobs AS synchronous
          # flink lanes: the gcp/orchestrator/run.sh Cloud Run job; beam: the Composer DAG
          DEFINE COMMUNICATION Load TO Target System Mock AS asynchronous VIA Kafka topic target-system-target
          DEFINE COMMUNICATION Target System Mock TO Recon AS asynchronous VIA Kafka topic target-system-confirmations
          DEFINE COORDINATION Orchestrated
          DEFINE CONSISTENCY Eventual
     # strict on the document schema, never on the wire protocol; idempotent on the account key
     DEFINE CONTRACT target-account AS spec/contracts/schemas/target-account.schema.json
          INCLUDING {accountId, customerId, productCode, currency, openedOn, status, balance, migration}
          WITH idempotency ON account_key

ASSERT(Communication between services matches the defined communication declarations) # [K12-1]
ASSERT(The run is led by its own orchestrator: gcp/orchestrator in the flink lanes, the Composer DAG in beam-dataflow) # [K12-2]